<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Petrobras June oil output up.</title>
<headline>Brazil Petrobras June oil output up.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consumption in Brazil of petroleum products averaged 1,682,500 barrels of oil per day (bpd) in June, up 1.91 percent on May's daily average, state oil monopoly Petrobras said in a statement.</p>
<p>The figure represents a 10.6-percent increase on June last year, Petrobras said.</p>
<p>Daily natural gas output stood at 16.7 million cubic meters in June, up from 16.2 million cubic meters in May and 15.2 million cubic meters in June 1996.</p>
<p>Of the total, diesel accounted for 549,100 bpd and gasoline for 311,700 bpd, Petrobras said.</p>
<p>((--Simona de Logu, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 507 4151))</p>
